        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 403.38,
          "end": 404.823,
          "en": "to add new expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "37143080",
      "title": "Using Icons & Formatting Dates",
      "lectureOrder": 105,
      "videoOrder": 96,
      "sourceHash": "a996e95b83a401bf1b0bbc146e594a9e6ce3099a4f0f05f52a8974910ac78772",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "Now for both the dynamic icon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 7.53,
          "en": "and the formatted date, I'll actually go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.53,
          "end": 10.32,
          "en": "to my expense start in the models folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 13.17,
          "en": "because in there I want to tweak the expense class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.17,
          "end": 16.89,
          "en": "to make outputting a formatted date a bit easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.89,
          "end": 19.68,
          "en": "And I want to add a new value to this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.68,
          "end": 23.133,
          "en": "So not to the expense class, but to the file as a whole.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.06,
          "end": 29.04,
          "en": "Here I want to add a constant value called category icons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.04,
          "end": 31.26,
          "en": "or the constant is called category icons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 35.94,
          "en": "And the values should be a map where the keys will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.94,
          "end": 38.46,
          "en": "category enum values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.46,
          "end": 39.54,
          "en": "And the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.54,
          "end": 43.35,
          "en": "of those keys in this map will be the actual icons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.35,
          "end": 46.8,
          "en": "that should be displayed for the different categories",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 49.59,
          "en": "so that in this expense dart file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.59,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "we don't just store the definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 54.48,
          "en": "of our expense value objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "but instead we also store the available categories",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 60.87,
          "en": "and the icons that belong to these categories.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.87,
          "end": 63.24,
          "en": "You could split this across multiple files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.24,
          "end": 65.43299999999999,
          "en": "but here I'll keep it all in one file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.99,
          "end": 71.34,
          "en": "So here my keys are these different enum values like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.34,
          "end": 73.833,
          "en": "category food with the dot notation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 78.57,
          "en": "And then the value set with a colon here in a map",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.57,
          "end": 82.77,
          "en": "as you learn before in this course would be an icon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.77,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "And here I'll use Flutter's built-in icons class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 88.83,
          "en": "which of course must be imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.83,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "So material dot dart from Flutter must be imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 97.5,
          "en": "And then here for food, I'll use the lunch dining icon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.5,
          "end": 100.17,
          "en": "And of course you can browse through all those icons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.17,
          "end": 101.97,
          "en": "and pick the icons you like most.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.97,
          "end": 104.43,
          "en": "But I'll use this one for the food category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.43,
          "end": 108.66,
          "en": "Then for the travel category, I'll use icons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.66,
          "end": 111.15299999999999,
          "en": "flight underscore takeoff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.43,
          "end": 118.083,
          "en": "For the leisure category, I'll use icons dot movie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.94,
          "end": 122.94,
          "en": "And for the last category, the work category,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.94,
          "end": 125.643,
          "en": "I'll use icons dot work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.03,
          "end": 130.5,
          "en": "So these are my icons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.5,
          "end": 133.38,
          "en": "and I'll soon use them here in expense item dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.38,
          "end": 137.223,
          "en": "But before we do that, I want to tweak this expense class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.21,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "This class at the moment is simply defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 143.91,
          "en": "to define the data structure of our expense objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.91,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "And this is of course very useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 148.95,
          "en": "because that allows us to create such expense objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.95,
          "end": 151.44,
          "en": "with ease and it gives us auto completion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.44,
          "end": 154.65,
          "en": "and type safety when working with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 157.82999999999998,
          "en": "But of course, you can not just store properties in classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.82999999999998,
          "end": 161.46,
          "en": "Instead, you can also add methods to classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.46,
          "end": 166.2,
          "en": "And here we could add a method called Get Formatted date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.2,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "though if you find yourself defining methods that start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 171.81,
          "en": "with get as a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.81,
          "end": 175.941,
          "en": "or that are in the end all about transforming one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.941,
          "end": 177.93,
          "en": "of these property values, you could, instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.93,
          "end": 181.69,
          "en": "of creating such a method, also create a so-called getter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.03,
          "end": 186.54,
          "en": "for that you use the special get keyword built into dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.54,
          "end": 188.31,
          "en": "and then the name of your getter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.31,
          "end": 190.95,
          "en": "which now should be named like any other property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.95,
          "end": 192.813,
          "en": "for example, formatted date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.71,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "And you should also define your return value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "So the type of value that will be produced by this getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 202.26,
          "en": "And you skip these parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.26,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "Instead, you just have opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 209.25,
          "en": "And between those curly braces, you return your value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.25,
          "end": 213.69,
          "en": "which should depend on your other property values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.69,
          "end": 217.3,
          "en": "And here I wanna reach out to my date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.64,
          "end": 221.73,
          "en": "property and format that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.73,
          "end": 226.05,
          "en": "Now formatting dates manually in Dart is quite cumbersome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.05,
          "end": 229.07999999999998,
          "en": "And for that reason we'll use another third party package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.07999999999998,
          "end": 232.3,
          "en": "here, the Intel INTL package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.31,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "for which you can simply search to find it on pub dev.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 240.39,
          "en": "And as always, you can learn more about this package here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240.39,
          "end": 242.49,
          "en": "It's a quite powerful package that can help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.49,
          "end": 244.89,
          "en": "with the localization as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.89,
          "end": 248.13,
          "en": "But here we'll use it to output a formatted date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.13,
          "end": 251.97,
          "en": "And for that we'll just add it to this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.97,
          "end": 254.463,
          "en": "a running Flutter pub at Intel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.45,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "And with it added in this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 263.16,
          "en": "expense dart file, we can import it just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 263.16,
          "end": 264.33,
          "en": "as we import it Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 264.33,
          "end": 268.2,
          "en": "or the UUID package by importing intel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 268.2,
          "end": 270.57,
          "en": "And then here the Intel Dart file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.57,
          "end": 272.64,
          "en": "That's what we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.64,
          "end": 274.98,
          "en": "And now with that package imported,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.98,
          "end": 279.12,
          "en": "we can use the date format class, which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.12,
          "end": 281.61,
          "en": "provided by this Intel package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.61,
          "end": 286.32,
          "en": "And there the YMD constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.32,
          "end": 287.79,
          "en": "and will store the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 287.79,
          "end": 291.69,
          "en": "of calling this constructor function in a final variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 291.69,
          "end": 293.24,
          "en": "that could be called formatter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.21,
          "end": 297.93,
          "en": "And YMD simply creates a formatter object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297.93,
          "end": 300.63,
          "en": "which we can then use to format dates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.63,
          "end": 303.63,
          "en": "So it's a utility object you could say, created with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.63,
          "end": 304.89,
          "en": "of the date format class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 304.89,
          "end": 307.2,
          "en": "and this special constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 307.2,
          "end": 309.18,
          "en": "provided by the Intel package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.18,
          "end": 312.12,
          "en": "And this YMD constructive function defines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 312.12,
          "end": 314.49,
          "en": "how the date will be formatted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 314.49,
          "end": 317.91,
          "en": "And indeed date format supports many constructive functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 317.91,
          "end": 320.61,
          "en": "that could be used to format dates in all kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 320.61,
          "end": 322.32,
          "en": "of different versions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 322.32,
          "end": 326.16,
          "en": "Y stands for a year, M for month and D four day,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 326.16,
          "end": 328.29,
          "en": "and YMD used like this is just one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 328.29,
          "end": 330.663,
          "en": "of those predefined formatting options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.53,
          "end": 334.2,
          "en": "So now we can use this formatter object down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 334.2,
          "end": 335.403,
          "en": "in this getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 337.11,
          "end": 341.04,
          "en": "And on that object you can call the format method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 341.04,
          "end": 343.023,
          "en": "and then pass your date to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 344.19,
          "end": 347.07,
          "en": "And this will return a string containing the formatted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.07,
          "end": 348.39,
          "en": "version of that date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.39,
          "end": 350.79,
          "en": "So the more human readable version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.79,
          "end": 353.01,
          "en": "And now with this formatted date added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.01,
          "end": 355.59000000000003,
          "en": "and this icon map added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 355.59000000000003,
          "end": 358.32,
          "en": "we can use this information here in expense item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 358.32,
          "end": 362.04,
          "en": "And for the icon here in this inner row, instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 362.04,
          "end": 366.24,
          "en": "of always using the hardcoded alarm, we can now reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 366.24,
          "end": 370.53,
          "en": "to our category icons map, which we have in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 370.53,
          "end": 371.733,
          "en": "that other file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 372.69,
          "end": 374.85,
          "en": "and use this square bracket notation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 374.85,
          "end": 378.18,
          "en": "to access a specific item in that map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.18,
          "end": 383.18,
          "en": "And since in that map we use Enum values as keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 383.88,
          "end": 386.67,
          "en": "We also have to use such a enum value as a key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 386.67,
          "end": 389.58,
          "en": "to access an icon, which is no problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 389.58,
          "end": 393.54,
          "en": "because in our expense object with which we're working here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 393.54,
          "end": 396.45,
          "en": "we have this category property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 396.45,
          "end": 400.563,
          "en": "which stores enum values of that category, enum.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 401.49,
          "end": 403.92,
          "en": "Now we also have to remove const here though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 403.92,
          "end": 406.74,
          "en": "because this isn't a const value anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 406.74,
          "end": 410.67,
          "en": "Instead, this is generated dynamically well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 410.67,
          "end": 411.75,
          "en": "and forward a date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 411.75,
          "end": 416.64,
          "en": "We now access expense, dot formatted date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 416.64,
          "end": 418.32,
          "en": "You don't add parentheses here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 418.32,
          "end": 420.93,
          "en": "because it's a getter, not a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 420.93,
          "end": 425.19,
          "en": "If you did define formatted date as a method instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 425.19,
          "end": 428.16,
